# NestFlow Project Context

NestFlow is an internal task-management system for Eden / Nest by Eden.

- Product name: NestFlow
- Planned URL: tasks.nestbyeden.app
- Tagline: Plan. Assign. Deliver.
- Primary brand colour: `#FF6300`
- Modes: light and dark

## Stack (approved)

- Next.js App Router + TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Supabase (Auth, Postgres, Realtime; shared NestByEden project)
- Cloudflare R2 (private NestFlow attachments; ADR-004)
- React Hook Form + Zod
- TanStack Table
- dnd-kit
- Motion for React (selective)
- Resend (email)
- Web Push API
- Vitest + Playwright
- Vercel deployment
- pnpm

## Roles

Administrator, Line Manager, HR, Staff.

## Documentation hierarchy

When documents disagree, prefer this order:

1. Approved ADR (`docs/decisions/`)
2. PRD (`docs/product/PRD.md`)
3. Architecture and database docs
4. Design and component docs
5. Coding rules and documentation style (`docs/engineering/CODING_RULES.md`, `docs/engineering/DOCS_STYLE.md`)
6. Roadmap / Tasks
7. `docs/memory/OBSIDIAN_MEMORY.md`

Memory summarises approved facts. It must never silently override source documents.

## Agent behaviour

- Read `docs/memory/OBSIDIAN_MEMORY.md` at the start of substantial work.
- Follow `docs/engineering/DOCS_STYLE.md` when editing docs (Apple Style Guide + DocC page shape).
- Prefer Server Components by default; Client Components only for interaction.
- Never expose the Supabase service-role key or R2 secrets to the browser.
- Don't invent product names, statuses, or roles outside the docs.
- Follow `docs/engineering/CODING_RULES.md` for implementation work.
